.TH str2u 3 (date) liba2i-(unreleased)
.
.
.SH Name
str2u,
str2uhh,
str2uh,
str2ui,
str2ul,
str2ull
\-
convert a string to an unsigned integer
.
.
.SH Library
String-to-integer library
.RI ( liba2i ,\~ \-la2i )
.
.
.SH Synopsis
.nf
.B #include <a2i/str2i/str2u.h>
.fi
.
.P
.B int
.SY str2u (
.B TYPE,
.BI TYPE\~*restrict\~ n ,
.BI const\~char\~* s );
.YS
.
.P
.B int
.SY str2uhh (
.BI unsigned\~char\~*restrict\~ n ,
.BI const\~char\~* s );
.YS .
.B int
.SY str2uh (
.BI unsigned\~short\~*restrict\~ n ,
.BI const\~char\~* s );
.YS .
.B int
.SY str2ui (
.BI unsigned\~int\~*restrict\~ n ,
.BI const\~char\~* s );
.YS .
.B int
.SY str2ul (
.BI unsigned\~long\~*restrict\~ n ,
.BI const\~char\~* s );
.YS .
.B int
.SY str2ull (
.BI unsigned\~long\~long\~*restrict\~ n ,
.BI const\~char\~* s );
.YS
.
.SH Description
These functions and macros
are convenience wrappers around
.MR a2u 3 ,
providing common defaults for the remaining arguments.
The base is 0;
the end pointer is NULL;
and the limits are those of the type.
.
.
.SH Examples
The following calls are all equivalent:
.P
.in +4n
.EX
str2ul(&n, s);
str2u(unsigned long, &n, s);
str2i(unsigned long, &n, s);
a2ul(&n, s, NULL, 0, 0, ULONG_MAX);
a2u(unsigned long, &n, s, NULL, 0, 0, ULONG_MAX);
a2i(unsigned long, &n, s, NULL, 0, 0, ULONG_MAX);
.EE
.in
.
.
.SH See also
.MR a2i 3 ,
.MR a2s 3 ,
.MR a2u 3 ,
.MR str2i 3 ,
.MR str2s 3
